 "notes": "Answers: license_type and transaction tick their box; 'Other: text' also writes the text. Escrow, bookkeeper and landlord take three lines each: name, address, telephone. funds takes up to eight lines, one per source: 'amount, type, source and terms' (the first two commas split the columns). banks takes up to two lines, 'bank name, bank address'; account numbers are never written by Placetta and stay for the applicant, as do items 13 to 15 (convictions and violations, which the applicant answers and explains), the P-12 licensee box and the section boxes under person-to-person transfers. 'None' leaves an optional line blank. The signature, date and attestation are left for the applicant and the ABC employee or notary.",
